## fastcompile-macros 11: no-fallback-front-ty: with 01358, the bridge's `run_client` closure has a call inference leaves typeless (every proc macro stops)

The 00:49 self-run (source /Volumes/Projects/.coord-1030/self-src-run0049b, which has 01358's hir-def edits; HEAD does not) stops every serde derive (26, log /tmp/blaze-lanes/self-0049.log) with `MirLowerErrorForClosure(<closure of FunctionId 2974b>, MissingFunctionDefinition(2974b, expr 17))`: a `Call` whose callee's type is `TyKind::Error` (hir-ty-mir `mir/lower.rs:1395`). Its stack, read by how the evaluator names frames (a closure frame by its owner): proc_macro `selfless_reify` `wrapper` (expr 5 = `f(bridge)`) -> `Client::expand1`'s closure (expr 4 = `run_client(bridge, f)`) -> `run_client` (expr 43 = `panic::catch_unwind(..)`) -> `std::panic::catch_unwind` -> `panicking::catch_unwind` -> `do_call`, which calls `run_client`'s `catch_unwind` closure. Expr 17 of `run_client` by my count is `<(ExpnGlobals<Span>, A)>::decode(reader, &mut ())` (client.rs:259), `A: for<'a, 's> Decode<'a, 's, ()>`: every `Decode` impl of the bridge leaves header lifetimes out (`impl<'a, S, A: for<'s> Decode<'a, 's, S>, B: ..> Decode<'a, '_, S> for (A, B)`, rpc.rs:197; `ExpnGlobals<Span>`'s from `compound_traits!`, rpc.rs:44; `impl<S> Decode<'_, '_, S> for Span`, client.rs:77). Before 01358 those `'_` were error regions, which hold for anything, so the probe matched; with fresh params it checks for real and something in it fails. That fits your bisection of the 84-crate stop to 01358.

The next self-run says exactly which call and why: blaze-macro-eval now renders a stop with names (`run/describe.rs`): the closure's function and `file:line:col`, the callee as written, and inference's `UnresolvedAssocItem`/`UnresolvedPath`/`UnresolvedIdent` for it.

A fixture for `impl_header_elided_lifetimes.rs` in the bridge's shapes (assert `run_client` has no diagnostics and its `decode` path resolves):

```rust
pub trait Decode<'a, 's, S>: Sized { fn decode(r: &mut &'a [u8], s: &'s mut S) -> Self; }
impl<S> Decode<'_, '_, S> for () { fn decode(_: &mut &[u8], _: &mut S) -> Self {} }
impl<'a, S, A: for<'s> Decode<'a, 's, S>, B: for<'s> Decode<'a, 's, S>> Decode<'a, '_, S> for (A, B) {
    fn decode(r: &mut &'a [u8], s: &mut S) -> Self { (Decode::decode(r, s), Decode::decode(r, s)) }
}
macro_rules! rpc_struct { (struct $name:ident <$T:ident> { $($field:ident),* }) => {
    pub struct $name<$T> { $(pub $field: $T),* }
    impl<'a, S, $T: for<'s> Decode<'a, 's, S>> Decode<'a, '_, S> for $name<$T> {
        fn decode(r: &mut &'a [u8], s: &mut S) -> Self { $name { $($field: Decode::decode(r, s)),* } }
    }
} }
pub struct Span(u32);
impl<S> Decode<'_, '_, S> for Span { fn decode(_: &mut &[u8], _: &mut S) -> Self { Span(0) } }
rpc_struct!(struct ExpnGlobals<Span> { def_site, call_site });
pub fn run_client<A: for<'a, 's> Decode<'a, 's, ()>>(buf: &[u8]) -> A {
    let f = || {
        let reader = &mut &buf[..];
        let (_globals, input) = <(ExpnGlobals<Span>, A)>::decode(reader, &mut ());
        input
    };
    f()
}
```

The end-to-end check is blaze-engine `tests/repro.rs` `a_struct_deriving_deserialize_reads_its_fields` (real serde 1.0.229, `--features llvm`).
